WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:02.525
This is CXAI by IVR Help.

00:00:02.575 --> 00:00:06.317
It works on the phone platform you already have.

00:00:06.367 --> 00:00:14.848
It answers routine calls with AI, shows exactly where callers give up, and checks every call for compliance.

00:00:14.898 --> 00:00:19.430
Here is how that looks in eight different contact centers.

00:00:20.717 --> 00:00:24.675
Summit Health Partners runs four clinics on Genesys Cloud.

00:00:24.725 --> 00:00:34.626
This morning, CXAI flagged that a third of callers in the Billing menu hang up between noon and two, most of them with simple balance questions.

00:00:34.676 --> 00:00:40.914
The practice manager approves an AI callback for that window, and the rule goes to Genesys.

00:00:40.964 --> 00:00:43.747
Nothing else in the phone system changes.

00:00:45.507 --> 00:00:48.316
Harborview Credit Union is on NICE CXone.

00:00:48.366 --> 00:01:00.029
Instead of reviewing one or two percent of calls, their compliance lead sees every call scored for identity verification, recording disclosure, and card data redaction.

00:01:00.079 --> 00:01:05.537
She filters to the flagged calls and builds an audit-ready report in one click.

00:01:07.482 --> 00:01:10.099
Crestline Mutual Insurance runs Five9.

00:01:10.149 --> 00:01:16.557
Routine requests like claim status and ID cards are answered by the AI agent, day and night.

00:01:16.607 --> 00:01:24.698
When a caller needs a person, CXAI hands them to the right team with the full context, so nobody repeats themselves.

00:01:24.748 --> 00:01:29.752
The counters at the top show calls resolved and staff hours saved today.

00:01:31.281 --> 00:01:33.935
Northwind Outfitters uses Zendesk Talk.

00:01:33.985 --> 00:01:45.791
Their support director opens the leader dashboard: calls the AI resolved, callers who no longer abandon, hours saved, and the trend over thirty days, across every channel.

00:01:47.382 --> 00:01:50.710
Bluewater Energy runs Cisco Webex Contact Center.

00:01:50.760 --> 00:01:56.914
CXAI spots a routing loop: callers in the Service menu keep landing back at the main menu.

00:01:56.964 --> 00:02:03.532
The operations manager pushes a loop-break rule, so callers reach a person instead of giving up.

00:02:05.024 --> 00:02:07.087
Seaside Resorts Group is on 8x8.

00:02:07.137 --> 00:02:19.174
The reservations supervisor uses the coaching view to compare each agent's handle time, first contact resolution, and compliance, then opens one agent's calls before their one-on-one.

00:02:21.212 --> 00:02:25.199
Lakewood County Services runs Google Cloud contact center AI.

00:02:25.249 --> 00:02:35.922
Their workforce planner sees calls by hour against the forecast and the agents scheduled, so it is clear which hours need more people and which the AI can absorb.

00:02:37.515 --> 00:02:40.120
ProComfort Home Services uses Nextiva.

00:02:40.170 --> 00:02:42.425
Connecting CXAI starts read-only.

00:02:42.475 --> 00:02:47.875
Their admin picks the platform, pastes one key, and CXAI tests the connection.

00:02:47.925 --> 00:02:52.905
Most teams finish in minutes, and nothing on the live call path changes.

00:02:54.089 --> 00:02:56.748
Want to see it on your own numbers?

